    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 23 tests pass, including `Cp14Tests` (the new membership-number test) and the related `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field as a derived, read-only property formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, following the existing pattern used for other derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since the DTOs are generated at build time by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin, this makes `OwnerDto` expose the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression targeting `membershipNumber` and a `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method that builds the value:\n   ```java\n   String yy = String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   return owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + yy;\n   ```\n\nThe `YY` uses the last two digits of the registration year, zero-padded (e.g. year 2007 \u2192 `07`, matching the test's `substring(2,4)` extraction and the spec example `SMI-0007-M26`). Both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already populated (by the service and controller respectively) before `toOwnerDto` runs, so the value is always well-formed.",
